          %p These definitions are important for defining the two notions of equality for categories:
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              of categories
            is a fully faithful equivalent-on-objects functor.
          %p
            An
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            is a fully faithful split essentially surjective functor. Equivalently, it is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:A \to B
            which has a left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
