                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2013/03/category_theory_in_homotopy_ty.html"} Category Theory in Homotopy Type Theory
            %li#Ahrens13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benedikt+Ahrens"}> Benedikt Ahrens
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Univalent categories and Rezk completion
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Ahrend-UnivalentCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Am%C3%A9lia+Liao"}> Amélia Liao
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Univalent Category Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+Electronic+Seminar+Talks"} Homotopy Type Theory Electronic Seminar Talks
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=asY6dXkR2yg"} video
          %p
            Implementation in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jason+Gross"}> Jason Gross
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Chlipala"} Adam Chlipala
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Spivak"} David Spivak
              = succeed "," do
                %em Experience Implementing a Performant Category-Theory Library in Coq
              %em Interactive Theorem Proving. ITP 2014
              Lecture Notes in Computer Science,
              %strong 8558
              Springer (2014)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1401.7694"} arXiv:1401.7694
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-08970-6_18"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-08970-6_18
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            code formalizing this includes the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/benediktahrens/rezk_completion"} github.com/benediktahrens/rezk_completion
          %p
            and in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+Agda"} cubical Agda
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1lab"}> 1lab
              \:
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://1lab.dev/Cat.Base.html"} Cat.Base
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2C1%29-categories"} (n,1)-categories
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#CapriottiKraus17
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Capriotti"}> Paolo Capriotti
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Kraus"} Nicolai Kraus
              %em Univalent Higher Categories via Complete Semi-Segal Types
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.03693"}> arXiv:1707.03693
              )
          %p and, by different means, in
          %ul
            %li#RiehlShulman17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"} Michael Shulman
                %em
                  A type theory for synthetic
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1705.07442"}> arXiv:1705.07442
                )
            %li#Riehl18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The synthetic theory of ∞-categories vs the synthetic theory of ∞-categories
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/vvmc2018"} Vladimir Voevodsky Memorial Conference 2018
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.jhu.edu/~eriehl/Voevodsky.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Formalization of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benedikt+Ahrens"}> Benedikt Ahrens
              , Dan Frumin, Marco Maggesi, Niels van der Weide,
              %em Bicategories in Univalent Foundations
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.01152"}> arXiv:1903.01152
              )
          %p Lemmas and proofs above are taken from:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013)
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalent+categories"} univalent categories
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kobe+Wullaert"}> Kobe Wullaert
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Matthes"} Ralph Matthes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benedikt+Ahrens"} Benedikt Ahrens
              %em Univalent Monoidal Categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03146"}> arXiv:2212.03146
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesCoinduction By coinduction
          %p
            A formalization in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT"} HoTT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
            of general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-categories"} (n,r)-categories
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n,r \in \mathbb{N} \sqcup \{\infty\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinductive+types"} coinductive types
            of infinity-graphs, with operations defined by induction-coinduction, is implemented in
          %ul
            %li#Morrison19
              Darin Morrison,
